# Derived by hand from Semantics R3 (a hold takes one write a tick: !either counts once in the owner in the click's tick) and ch. 9 as ruled (an event output answers the child's place as an input of the next tick, which is owed: both child buttons hear !either in the compute tick, the child's merge takes its left, one hit).
test the_owner_is_woken_again

tick 0
  added:
    0: Ui.Button(label="go")
    1: Ui.Button(label="other")
    2/[2]/0: Ui.Label(text="0 hits")
    3: Ui.Label(text="0")

tick 1
  in:
    0: click
  changed:
    3: Ui.Label(text="1")

tick 2
  changed:
    2/[2]/0: Ui.Label(text="1 hits")

tick 3
  in:
    1: click
  changed:
    3: Ui.Label(text="2")

tick 4
  changed:
    2/[2]/0: Ui.Label(text="2 hits")
